            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Tamil for a locality, then the Tamil for a centre."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: சதுக்கம்",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சதுக்கம் — catukkam — \"a town square\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சதுக்கத்தில் நிறைய மக்கள் கூடியிருந்தார்கள். catukkattil niṟaiya makkaḷ kūṭiyiruntārkaḷ. Many people had gathered in the square."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before a case the -அம் becomes -அத்து-: சதுக்கத்தில்."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "சதுக்கம் (catukkam) is borrowed from Prakrit catukka, \"a set of four, a crossroads, a village square\", from Sanskrit catuṣka (CDIAL 4629)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
